    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1060-a1">

                <pb facs="0824" n="742" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg742"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Embassy to the Minister for Foreign
                        Affairs</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Note verbale.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-11-28"><hi rendition="#italic">November 28,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 133.]</seg></opener>
                <p>The embassy of the United States has the honor again to draw the attention of the
                    Sublime Porte to its note verbale of the 28th of September last, relating to the
                    ease of Mr. Telford Erickson, to which no reply has been received.</p>
                <p>This embassy has received instructions from the Government of the United States
                    to point out to the Ottoman Government that the attitude of the local
                    authorities in this case is considered as arbitrary, violating directly existing
                    rights, and, in consequence, while reserving to the Government of the United
                    States every right in relation to the question of damages, to urgently insist
                    that the present restrictions against the return of Mr. Erickson to Elbassan
                    should be immediately withdrawn.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
